problem:
Problem description
- There is a finite planning horizon $$\mathcal{T}$$ of ordered periods indexed by $$t$$, and a set of products $$\mathcal{P}$$ indexed by $$p$$.
- The original instance contains one product, but the structure is written in a general multi-product form.
- Initial on-hand inventory is given by $$I^0_p$$ for each product $$p \in \mathcal{P}$$.
- Storage is limited by a warehouse capacity $$C$$, and the total inventory kept in storage must never exceed this limit at any time.
- Unit purchase costs are given by $$c^b_{p,t}$$ for each product-period pair, and unit selling revenues are given by $$c^s_{p,t}$$.
- Purchases are made at the beginning of each period, and sales are made during that same period.
- Inventory that is not sold in a period carries forward to the next period.
- The planning goal is to choose how much to purchase and how much to sell in each period so that the total net financial return over the planning horizon is as large as possible.
- Required business rules:
  - purchase quantities must be nonnegative;
  - sales quantities must be nonnegative;
  - sales in any period can only come from inventory available after that period’s purchases;
  - ending inventory in each period must remain nonnegative;
  - inventory in storage must stay within the warehouse capacity;
  - if an optional exogenous sales cap $$D_{p,t}$$ is provided, sales must also respect that cap.
- A solution is represented by:
  - $$x_{p,t}$$: quantity purchased for product $$p$$ at the beginning of period $$t$$;
  - $$y_{p,t}$$: quantity sold for product $$p$$ during period $$t$$;
  - $$s_{p,t}$$: ending inventory of product $$p$$ after period $$t$$;
  - $$Z$$: total net revenue achieved over the full planning horizon.

Input Format
{
  "time_horizon": {
    "count": "$$T$$",
    "period_labels": "ordered list of length $$T$$"
  },
  "products": {
    "count": "$$P$$",
    "labels": "ordered list of length $$P$$"
  },
  "initial_inventory": {
    "shape": "$$P$$",
    "meaning": "starting inventory vector $$I^0_p$$ for each product $$p$$"
  },
  "storage_capacity": {
    "shape": "$$1$$",
    "meaning": "warehouse capacity parameter $$C$$"
  },
  "purchase_price": {
    "shape": "$$P \\times T$$",
    "meaning": "unit purchase cost matrix $$c^b_{p,t}$$"
  },
  "selling_price": {
    "shape": "$$P \\times T$$",
    "meaning": "unit selling revenue matrix $$c^s_{p,t}$$"
  },
  "optional_demand_cap": {
    "shape": "$$P \\times T$$",
    "meaning": "optional sales-limit matrix $$D_{p,t}$$ if the application includes one; otherwise omitted"
  }
}

Output Format
{
  "purchase_quantity": {
    "shape": "$$P \\times T$$",
    "ordering": "aligned with the input period order",
    "meaning": "purchase plan $$x_{p,t}$$"
  },
  "sales_quantity": {
    "shape": "$$P \\times T$$",
    "ordering": "aligned with the input period order",
    "meaning": "sales plan $$y_{p,t}$$"
  },
  "ending_inventory": {
    "shape": "$$P \\times T$$",
    "ordering": "aligned with the input period order",
    "meaning": "ending inventory plan $$s_{p,t}$$"
  },
  "total_net_revenue": {
    "shape": "$$1$$",
    "meaning": "objective value $$Z$$ achieved by the plan"
  }
}

Example(s)

Input 1
{
  "time_horizon": {
    "count": 6,
    "period_labels": ["July", "August", "September", "October", "November", "December"]
  },
  "products": {
    "count": 1,
    "labels": ["product_1"]
  },
  "initial_inventory": [200],
  "storage_capacity": 500,
  "purchase_price": [[28, 24, 25, 27, 23, 23]],
  "selling_price": [[29, 24, 26, 28, 22, 25]]
}
